              Digital Equipment Corporation and Anixter
               Build West Coast Network for Cybersmith


MAYNARD, Mass., October 29, 1996 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
today announced that Cybersmith, a pioneer in cybercafes, has chosen 
Digital networking products to provide savvy, computer literate 
users with high-speed T1 Internet access and video conferencing. 
Cybersmith's state-of-the-art Internet applications and demanding 
users depend on network reliability and superior performance 
provided by Digital's networking products.

     Cybersmith's new, premier Palo Alto store, in the heart of 
Silicon Valley, is the company's first West Coast location and will 
serve as a network hub for other planned West Coast openings. The 
new location is ideal for conducting various computer training and 
events for business executives.

     "By using Digital's enterprise networking solutions, Cybersmith 
is providing users with the highest level of Internet connectivity 
that is typically unavailable in most small offices and homes," said 
Bill Hawe, technical director for Digital's Network Product Business.  
"The DEChub product family was designed to meet the increasing 
network needs of distributed enterprises, such as Cybersmith."

     Cybersmith has chosen Digital for its network, based on 
investment protection, flexibility, redundancy and modularity 
provided by Digital's solutions. The company uses Digital's flagship 
DEChub family of products to connect users within its stores' LANs 
to the Internet. The DEChub products work as both standalone hubs 
and chassis-based modules, providing investment protection and 
flexibility. In addition, the family provides a protocol-independent 
backplane, supporting ATM, Ethernet, Fast Ethernet and FDDI, and 
includes hot-swap and redundant power features, providing undaunted 
performance.

     "Digital's solutions have helped us to sustain the leadership 
position in our market and have given us the flexibility to grow our 
network and implement cutting edge technologies as we expand to new 
locations," said Cybersmith vice president Jed Smith.

     Anixter Inc., a strategic partner of Digital Equipment 
Corporation and the value-added provider chosen by Cybersmith, 
packages Digital products for Cybersmith and currently provides 
integration support for the company. Anixter will facilitate the 
delivery and set-up of networking equipment for future store 
openings.

     "With the growth of Internet usage and multimedia 
communications for training and other business activities, Anixter 
is excited to provide the service and support for state-of-the-art 
networking solutions to our West Coast customers, such as 
Cybersmith," said Sherwood Robins, executive vice president of 
sales and marketing for Anixter.

     Cybersmith is committed to providing understanding, hands-on 
experience and technological information within an atmosphere of 
comfort and fun. The store's motto, "Explore, Create, Compete, 
Connect," points to the new person-to-person, not person-to-machine, 
interaction with computers. Cybersmith is the latest brainchild of 
Marshall Smith, acting president of Cybersmith and founder of 
Paperback Booksmith, Videosmith and Learningsmith stores, and his 
son, Jed Smith, who has five years of Silicon Valley experience. For 
more information, visit Cybersmith's World Wide Web site at 
http://.www.cybersmith.com.

     Anixter Inc., is a value-added provider of integrated 
networking and cabling solutions that support business information 
and network infrastructure requirements. Anixter teams with 
customers to implement these solutions by combining a variety of 
customized pre- and post-sale services, products from the world's 
leading manufacturers, and superior logistics management through a 
global network of 170 locations. Founded in 1957, Anixter is 
headquartered in the Chicago area. For more information, visit 
Anixter's World Wide Web site at http://www.anixter.com.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is a world leader in open client/
server solutions from personal computing to integrated worldwide 
information systems. Digital's scalable Intel and Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace.
