            Digital on Solid Ground -- and in the Air --
                          at Fall COMDEX'96


        Windows NT Enterprise Solutions, the Power of Alpha,
       AltaVista Airship Dominate DIGITAL's Presence at COMDEX


MAYNARD, Mass., Nov. 5, 1996 --  Digital Equipment Corporation will 
arrive at Fall COMDEX '96 with its broad range of industry-leading 
solutions for rapidly emerging Windows NT enterprise and Internet 
requirements -- with a twist that marks a first for both DIGITAL and 
COMDEX. 

DIGITAL will debut the AltaVista airship in flights over the Las 
Vegas Convention Center during the day and over "The Strip" at 
night.  The airship, traveling from Massachusetts to Las Vegas 
during the two weeks prior to the opening of the show, will arrive 
in time to inaugurate a brand-new venue for COMDEX exhibit 
demonstrations. 
	  
And on the ground, visitors to DIGITAL's booths in the Convention 
Center will be able to check out and participate in exhibits and 
demos -- with customers and partners -- that showcase the company's 
ability to help enterprise customers develop, deploy, manage, 
migrate and integrate Windows-based solutions more quickly and 
completely than any other vendor.

GET CONNECTED

Booth L4402, North Hall, LVCC

DIGITAL will demonstrate the company's unique strengths and 
capabilities as a provider of Windows enterprise solutions on both 
Intel and Alpha platforms.  Attendees will have an opportunity to 
GET CONNECTED with DIGITAL's latest technology offerings and test 
drive powerful new products designed and optimized for Windows 
NT-based applications. 

DIGITAL will showcase its full line of PC client/server solutions -- 
ranging from a new Prioris family of aggressively priced, single- 
and dual-processor Pentium Pro servers optimized for Windows NT 4.0 
Server to the company's enterprise-ready Venturis and Celebris 
desktop line-up and HiNote Ultra II and HiNote VP 500 mobile clients 
running Windows NT 4.0 Workstation.  Visitors should look for a 
DIGITAL PC Family presentation on connecting Windows NT to the 
Enterprise in the booth's Enterprise Computing Theater.  

Demos also will include high-availability DIGITAL Clusters for 
Windows NT on AlphaServer systems and on Digital StorageWorks 
Solutions; Multivendor StorageWorks Solution with RAID Array 450 
dual controllers on a SUN SPARC20 running Solaris 2.5; and a 
UNIX/Windows NT demo showing seamless interoperability among Digital 
UNIX, Windows NT and Windows 95 in a manufacturing environment.  
                                  
In addition, three demos running on Digital's Windows NT Personal 
Workstations will feature flight simulation by 3DFX; 3D on the Web, 
a client/server VRML demo with an AlphaServer system and Personal 
Workstation client, both running Windows NT and featuring Powerstorm 
Graphics; and Studio MAX by Kinetix, a 3D modeling application 
running on the new Pentium Pro Digital Personal Workstation 200i.

The Interactive Internet Theater will highlight the Internet 
Cyberbrew test-drive demo showcasing emerging Internet/Intranet 
technologies for electronic commerce, security and workgroup 
collaboration.

DIGITAL SEMICONDUCTOR

Booth L4602, North Hall, LVCC

Alpha's superior performance and momentum in the Windows NT market 
will be dramatically highlighted by the activities of more than a 
dozen Alpha chip customers and technology partners.  Electronics 
giants Mitsubishi Electric and Samsung Electronics join a host of 
system and component manufacturers to demonstrate new and 
forthcoming systems, ranging from under-$3,000 PCs to dual-processor 
500 MHz workstations.  A "test drive" area for Digital FX!32 
software, winner of last year's BYTE magazine "Best New Technology" 
award, demonstrates Alpha's superior performance for all 32-bit 
Windows applications.

DIGITAL's growing merchant vendor business is further evident in the 
booth's Emerging Technologies areas, comprising demonstrations of 
Apple Computer's recently announced MessagePad 2000 handheld 
computer and Internet appliances from WYSE Technology, Boundless, 
Inc., and Lucky Gold Star, each of which uses the StrongARM SA-110 
high-speed, low-power microprocessor.  DIGITAL's PCI peripheral 
chips will also be demonstrated in practical solutions for PC-based 
videoconferencing, real-time video compression, and system 
expandability through PCI-to-PCI bridging.

DIGITAL PARTNER PAVILION

Booth L4202, North Hall, LVCC

Sponsored by DIGITAL and its Association of Software and Application 
Partners (ASAP), the booth will showcase leading providers of 
complete business solutions on DIGITAL's high-performance platforms.  

DIGITAL and Microsoft will preview enterprise technologies that 
demonstrate the clear customer benefits of the Microsoft and Digital 
Alliance for Enterprise Computing -- most notably the enterprise
scalability and reliability of Windows NT enabled by the combination 
of an AlphaServer 8000 series enterprise system and a one-terabyte

StorageWorks Solution running Windows NT 4.0 and the Microsoft SQL 
Server 6.5 database.  This "technology preview" will include several 
commercial, technical and Internet applications. 

Software developers can learn more about the valuable technical and 
marketing assistance programs available from ASAP by coming to the 
Partner Information Desk in the booth.

THE ALTAVISTA AIRSHIP

Overhead (and Hilton Hotel Meeting Rooms H10, H12)

Finally, not to be overlooked, and equipped with an air-to-ground 
Internet link, the 130-foot-long AltaVista Airship will demonstrate 
the power of AltaVista OnSite Computing to do business from wherever 
business takes place -- even from 5,000 feet in the air.

AltaVista will demonstrate the AltaVista Forum, AltaVista Search 
Private eXtension (PX) and AltaVista Tunnel products in meeting 
rooms at the Las Vegas Hilton (H10, H12).  AltaVista Forum V2.0 is 
the newest release of the award-winning Internet/Intranet 
collaboration product.  AltaVista Search PX extends the strength of 
the AltaVista Search public service on the Web to private domains, 
quickly and accurately locating information on Intranets and 
desktops.  AltaVista Tunnel allows remote workers to create a 
virtual private network by providing secure access through corporate 
firewalls using public Internet services.


ABOUT DIGITAL

Digital Equipment Corporation is a world leader in open client/
server solutions from personal computing to integrated worldwide 
information systems.  Digital's scalable Alpha and Intel platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace. 

