            AltaVista Search My Computer PX Announced --
         Finding Information On Desktops Simplified at Last


     ... Award-winning AltaVista Search Technology Moves OnSite
              from the World Wide Web to the Desktop...


MAYNARD, Mass., November 6, 1996 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
today announced the availability of AltaVista Search My Computer 
Private eXtension (PX) software, a fast and powerful solution to 
searching and indexing information on the desktop.  With AltaVista 
Search My Computer PX, finding information inside Windows 95 and 
Windows NT documents on PCs is as quick and easy as finding 
information with AltaVista on the Internet. AltaVista Search My 
Computer PX is priced at $29.95, and will be available for down-
loading on the Web at http://altavista.software.digital.com on
December 5, or from resellers beginning December 16.  Until November 
18, a special price of $19.95 is available for AltaVista Visionary 
Club members on the Web at http://altavista.software.digital.com/
blimp.html.

     Using the same web browser interface and powerful technology 
that drives the award-winning AltaVista Internet search service, 
which now receives over 20 million queries per day, AltaVista Search 
My Computer PX gives Internet/intranet users a simple, extremely 
fast tool for finding information within their public or private 
domains.  With a single click of an on-screen button, users can 
seamlessly search from the World Wide Web to their PC and back again 
in seconds without changing applications or learning new interfaces.  

     "With the phenomenal growth of the Internet and private 
intranets, finding critical information can be slow and difficult," 
said Ilene H. Lang, vice president of Digital's Internet Software 
Business Unit. "AltaVista Search My Computer PX is fast and easy.  
If the information's out there on the Web or in your private 
domains, AltaVista Search will find it for you.  AltaVista OnSite 
Computing means doing business wherever you are, and the first step 
is quickly finding the data you need."

     "I'm very impressed with this product," said Andrew Schlein,
Ph.D., director of Information Technology and Systems for the Queens
Borough Public Library in Jamaica, NY.  "I think that AltaVista 
Search My Computer Private eXtension is one of the most powerful 
utilities available for executives who rely more and more heavily on 
their desktop systems for productivity and time savings."

     According to Steve Fishman, chief information officer of 
Ultrasonic Precisions, Inc. of Ft. Lauderdale, FL, searching for a 
particular spreadsheet file "would have literally taken me hours 
'the old fashioned way.'"  Using AltaVista Search My Computer PX, he 
"searched for the contents of one of the cells, and within seconds, 
it had found the spreadsheet. Truly astonishing!"

     With AltaVista Search My Computer PX, individuals can 
automatically build a full word index of all HTML documents and more 
than 200 file types stored on their local PC and shared network 
drives, including applications from Microsoft, Lotus, Word Perfect 
and Eudora.  Navigating with the familiar AltaVista Search interface, 
users can find all documents, files, and email messages and attachments 
containing a selected search term.  

     Within seconds, the program's powerful query engine produces 
search results, including ranking information.  Clicking on a 
document in the AltaVista index automatically opens both the 
document and its launch application.  The index is stored locally, 
giving users access to searching when the system is not connected 
to a network.  The program can be scheduled to update the index at 
predetermined times, or upon request by the user.

     AltaVista Search My Computer PX includes an automated 
installation, making setup fast and easy.  The indexer can also be 
scheduled by the Windows 95 System Agent, providing a visual or 
audible indicator when it finishes building an index.  It supports 
popular application types, including Microsoft Word, Excel and 
PowerPoint documents, and Microsoft Exchange and Eudora ProV3.0 
email messages.

     AltaVista OnSite Computing solutions provide secure, simple 
and direct access to information and people over the Internet and 
private intranets.  AltaVista Search, Tunnel, Firewall, Forum, 
Directory and Mail products give users the competitive edge, 
enabling productive business to take place from anywhere.  Further 
information on AltaVista OnSite Computing is available at 
http://altavista.software.digital.com, or calling 800-336-7890.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is a world leader in open client/
server solutions from personal computing to integrated worldwide
information systems.  Digital's scalable Alpha and Intel platforms,
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace.
