                 Digital Reduces Prices, Adds Power
                  to Midrange AlphaServer Systems 
 
   
 ... Nearly 30% Cost Savings, Faster Processors, Twice the Memory ...


MAYNARD, Mass., November 7, 1996 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
today dramatically reduced prices and enhanced the performance of 
its record-breaking midrange AlphaServer RISC family of 64-bit 
application, database, and Internet/intranet systems.

     "Today we are offering customers even greater value in the 
volume segment of the AlphaServer line-up," said Pauline Nist, vice 
president of AlphaServer Business. "While other vendors are busy 
trying to introduce parts of a 64-bit platform, Digital continues to 
offer the industry's only complete 64-bit solution -- systems, 
operating systems, and applications. Today we are widening this lead 
with more attractive prices at the sweet spot of the AlphaServer 
product line."     

Significant Cost Reductions 

     Digital unveiled significantly reduced prices for AlphaServer 
4000 and 4100 midrange systems, the result of lower memory prices.
For example, end-user costs of AlphaServer 4100 5/400 Windows NT 
systems are down by as much as 25%, beginning at $38,040. 
AlphaServer 4000 systems offer similar savings. For example, 
AlphaServer 4000 5/300 systems are priced beginning at $30,040, a 
23% reduction. 

     In addition, AlphaServer 4000, 4100 and 2000 customers can save 
significantly on high quality add-on memory modules, with prices 
reduced by up to 29%. 

Significant Power Enhancements

     The company also increased the top-end performance of its 
widely deployed AlphaServer 2000 systems and the new 2100A LP 
midrange systems. Both systems are now available with Alpha 21164 
5/375 processor models. The 5/375 CPU provides industry-leading 
performance of 14.4 SPECfp95 and 11.6 SPECint95. Add-on memory 
prices for the AlphaServer 2000 systems were also reduced, by 20%.

     The new AlphaServer 2000 models are binary compatible with the 
other members of the AlphaServer family, and are covered by 
Digital's superior three-year onsite hardware warranty. All systems 
now contain a high-performance, 7200 RPM, 4.3 GB disk drive as 
standard equipment.

     In addition, all AlphaServer 4000 and 4100 systems are now 
available with twice the memory capacity of earlier versions. With 
new, more attractively priced 2 GB memory modules, the two-CPU 
AlphaServer 4000 systems now have a 4 GB memory capacity, while the 
four-CPU AlphaServer 4100 systems offer up to 8 GB of memory.

     AlphaServer 4000 and 4100 systems offer customers the 
industry's first midrange server platform with 64-bit Very-Large 
Memory (VLM64) capacity. Pioneered in Digital's high-end AlphaServer 
8000 enterprise systems, VLM64 provides industry-leading database 
performance and affordability. 

     For example, running Oracle Rdb7 for OpenVMS, the AlphaServer 
4100 5/400 system performs at 7985 tpmC at $174/tpmC. the 
AlphaServer 4100 5/400 system running Digital UNIX and Sybase SQL 
Server performs at 7598 tpmC at $152 per tpmC. 

     In addition, a two-processor AlphaServer 4000 provides the 
industry's highest midrange Internet server performance, as measured 
by the SPECweb96 industry-standard benchmark. All AlphaServer 
systems, including the AlphaServer 4000 family, ship with bundled 
Internet software on all operating systems, an industry first. 

     The industry-standard modular design of the AlphaServer 
4000/4100 platform enables VARs to order modules and configure 
systems themselves. Unbundling a system enables distributors to buy 
building blocks in advance, ensuring immediate availability of 
AlphaServer systems for their customers. 

     AlphaServer 4000/4100 and 2000 systems support Digital UNIX, 
OpenVMS, and Windows NT Server software environments.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is a world leader in open client/
server solutions from personal computing to integrated worldwide 
information systems.  Digital's scalable Alpha and Intel platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace. 
