       Digital's New Prioris HX 6000 Series of SMP Application
          Servers Provide Best Value at Breakthrough Prices


   Servers And Software Optimized For High-Performance, Networked
          Applications For Windows NT Across The Enterprise


MAYNARD, Mass., Nov. 11, 1996 -- Digital Equipment Corporation today 
unveiled its new Prioris HX 6000 series of 200 MHz Pentium Pro-based 
application servers designed to deliver unequaled enterprise-quality 
manageability, availability, performance and scalability at 
compelling new price points, starting at $6,000.

     "We're right on track with our goal to be the undisputed 
solutions provider for Windows NT across the enterprise," said Bruce 
Claflin, vice president and general manager of DIGITAL's Personal 
Computer Business Unit.  "The new Prioris HX 6000 series is targeted 
at users of value-driven, business-critical applications in 
departmental or geographically dispersed sites, especially in the 
commercial and government sectors, where Windows NT-based 
application demand is growing rapidly."

     The company also announced today the immediate availability of 
the latest Intel Pentium processor models of the Prioris LX and 
Prioris XL server series.  In addition, Lotus Notes failover support 
for DIGITAL Clusters for Windows NT; a turnkey RAID Cluster Kit; and 
enhanced cluster and management software were announced.  The company 
also said Windows NT 4.0 drivers for the HiNote Ultra II and HiNote 
VP 500 are available.

     DIGITAL's four new Prioris HX 6000 single and dual processor 
SMP application servers deliver exceptional value in manageability, 
availability, performance, scalability and dependable service.  With 
256KB and 512KB L2 cache variants, the new servers offer not only 
investment protection, but also choice not compromise.  Optimized 
for Microsoft's Windows NT Server, the new models are ideal for 
small, medium and large businesses and workgroups, as well as remote 
sites and branch offices of large companies who want to economically 
implement the latest applications across the enterprise.

     "The new two-way Prioris HX 6000 server series offers our 
customers the same award-winning features as our four-way Prioris ZX 
6000 series -- optimized 32-bit SMP performance, innovative 
clustering and server management technologies, to name a few, but at 
a lower cost of ownership with performance improvements of more than 
100 percent compared to equivalent Pentium-based systems," said 
Howard Elias, vice president, worldwide business segments for 
DIGITAL's PC Business.

Reducing Enterprise Cost of Ownership - System and 
Workgroup Manageability

     As with all Prioris servers, each Prioris HX 6000 server 
includes at no extra cost DIGITAL's ServerWORKS Manager, an easy-to-
use software package that simplifies workgroup and system management 
for LAN administrators, especially in mixed environments supporting 
NetWare, Windows NT Server, UNIX and OS/2 servers.  ServerWORKS 
Manager also allows single-console SNMP-based management of servers, 
clients, hubs, routers and printers through an intuitive interface.  
DIGITAL also enhanced its ServerWORKS Quick Launch installation and 
configuration utility to save customers hours of installation by 
auto-replicating customized server configurations in distributed 
computing environments.

     Through the innovative design and use of inter-integrated 
circuit technology in the Prioris HX 6000 series, DIGITAL's built-in 
Intelligent Server Management allows proactive, real-time monitoring 
of critical subsystems, such as CPUs, main logic board, RAID, fans, 
power supplies and memory to provide system administrators with 
up-to-the-minute status and alerting for business-critical servers 
via ServerWORKS Manager.

     For fast and accurate field service and parts inventory 
management, the company enhanced its server asset management and 
serviceability feature with built-in electronic identification and 
tracking.  In addition, DIGITAL's Remote Server Manager option 
provides wide area server management and control for remote or 
distributed sites.

High Availability Application Services

     The new Prioris HX servers include optional support for the 
industry-leading DIGITAL Clusters for Windows NT, a layered software 
application on top of Windows NT Server, which allows for the 
coupling of two DIGITAL servers through a shared SCSI bus and 
external storage. Both servers are capable of processing individual 
workloads but are managed and accessed by Windows clients as a 
single server.

     With DIGITAL Clusters for Windows NT, system failures and 
preventive maintenance become transparent to end-users, allowing 
them to remain productive through failovers and failbacks, without 
sacrificing availability.

     The company also said failover and failback support for Lotus 
Notes is now included with DIGITAL Clusters for Windows NT, 
providing high availability for Lotus Notes databases.

     In a class of its own, the affordable Prioris HX 6000 series 
comes standard with ECC memory, hot swap drives, a real-time 
diagnostic display panel, and redundant fans for maximum uptime with 
high availability options, including a redundant power supply, PCI 
RAID with battery backup for cache, and Remote Server Manager.

Optimized Performance for Networked Business Applications

     The new systems are designed from the ground up as 
business-critical application servers for resource-intensive 
applications, such as medium to large databases, Internet/intranet 
servers, messaging, groupware and communications gateways.  
Available with the fastest and most scalable 200MHz Pentium Pro 
processor, the systems also include up to 512KB of secondary
cache standard, with integrated dual Ultra-Wide SCSI controllers, 
integrated PCI Fast Ethernet and graphics, advanced memory 
interleaving -- all optimized for 32-bit SMP-enabled, networked 
application services on Windows NT Server or UNIX.

     Like the rest of the Prioris family, the new systems support a 
wide range of operating environments, including Windows NT Server, 
SCO UNIX products, Novell NetWare OS/2 and Banyan Vines.  DIGITAL 
also endorses the new I2O standard, which will provide increased 
performance and reduced costs in implementing hardware device 
drivers in the future.

Investment Protection - System Scalability and Expandability

     The Prioris HX 6000 series strengthens the company's scalable 
Intel and Alpha product families with its single and dual processor 
configurations, a choice of 256KB or 512KB (for at least a 25 
percent performance improvement) secondary cache sizes, up to 1GB of 
EDO ECC-protected memory, 63 GB of internal storage, (1TB external) 
and 11 expansion slots, and is I2O ready. Customers gain 80 percent 
more I/O expandability and 150 percent more storage capacity over 
competitive systems.  Debuting in the company's new frost white 
chassis, the Prioris HX 6000 is housed in a wide tower case, 
designed for serviceability and expansion.

Services

     DIGITAL's complete line of PC servers are backed by a three 
year on-site warranty, with next-business day response standard from 
authorized DIGITAL Warranty Service Providers and DIGITAL's 
Multivendor Customer Services organization. In addition, the company 
offers a number of service packages, including the DIGITAL Priority 
Service Plan, which provides a set of packaged services -- Priority, 
Priority-Plus, and Priority-Premier -- designed to meet availability 
requirements for a wide range of customers.

Windows NT 4.0 for Mobile Clients

     Continuing the company's leadership in making Windows NT-based 
mobile computing a practical reality for enterprise customers, 
Digital announced today availability of Windows NT 4.0 drivers 
across its full line of recently introduced HiNote mobile clients -- 
the HiNote Ultra II and HiNote VP 500.  The driver kits include exclusive 
advancements developed by DIGITAL to deliver unprecedented Windows NT 
performance on a notebook computer.  These include enhanced power 
management for extended battery life under Windows NT 4.0 and 
plug-and-play-like features, such as hot-docking support for system 
expansion options and selected PC Cards.

     The HiNote Ultra II and HiNote VP 500 Windows NT 3.51 and 4.0 
drivers can be obtained through DIGITAL's Internet Home Page or 
Bulletin Board System.  DIGITAL was the first in the industry to 
offer pre-loaded and pre-configured Windows NT mobile client 
solutions within the company's award-winning HiNote Ultra II family 
of thin, lightweight notebook computers.  DIGITAL is now making the 
same level of industry-leading Windows NT 4.0 notebook functionality 
available to its installed base of HiNote Ultra II and HiNote VP 500 
users as they migrate to the Windows NT operating system.

Pricing/Availability

     All of the new Prioris PC servers are available immediately.  
Estimated street prices for the Prioris HX 6000 series range from US 
$6,000 to $10,000, based on configuration.  Estimated street prices 
for the Prioris LX 5200 and Prioris XL 5200 servers are US $2,800 to 
$4,000 and US $3,000 to $5,000, respectively.  The RAID Cluster Kit 
has an estimated street price of US $8,500.  All of DIGITAL's PC 
servers are available through DIGITAL's channel partners, including 
master resellers, wholesalers, distributors, dealers, VARs and 
system integrators.  For complete pricing information, please refer 
to the attached Prioris Server fact sheets or call 1-800-DIGITAL.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is a world leader in open client/
server solutions from personal computing to integrated worldwide 
information systems.  DIGITAL's scalable Alpha and Intel platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace.
