                 Digital Extends AllConnect Program
                   with New Products to Facilitate
         Integration of Windows NT and OpenVMS Environments


 New Capabilities of Affinity Wave 3 Reinforce Digital's Leadership
         Position Providing Enterprise Windows NT Solutions


ANAHEIM, Calif., November 11, 1996 -- Digital Equipment Corporation
today announced significant new capabilities for Affinity for 
OpenVMS, part of Digital's AllConnect Program for Windows NT 
integration across the enterprise.  Digital is now delivering the 
third wave of new and enhanced products that allow customers of its 
OpenVMS operating system to more easily integrate Microsoft Windows 
NT(r) into their enterprise computing environments, as well as 
develop, deploy and manage applications across Windows NT and 
OpenVMS.  

     With these new additions to Affinity for OpenVMS, Digital 
introduces the latest wave of software that makes it easier for 
developers, users, and managers to take advantage of the 
high-performance, scalability, and bullet-proof availability of 
OpenVMS servers and OpenVMS cluster systems from within a Windows NT 
environment. 

     Announced today at the 35th Anniversary Digital Equipment 
Computer Users Society (DECUS) conference in Anaheim, Calif., are 
the following products that are part of the Affinity for OpenVMS 
Program:

     *	24 x 365 Computing: OpenVMS 7.1 -- Provides new support for 
        the high-speed Memory Channel(tm) cluster interconnect, 
        which delivers memory-to-memory communications with near-SMP 
        performance -- up to twice as fast as other available 
        cluster interconnects.

     *	Data Warehouse Solutions: Data Warehousing on OpenVMS -- 
        Provides operating system support including Very Large 
        Memory (VLM64)/Very Large Database (VLDB) for relational 
        database and data warehouse vendors such as Oracle, Sybase, 
        SAS Institute, IBI, Software AG and Microsoft.

     *	Windows NT Integration:  Enterprise Integration Server for 
        OpenVMS; Enterprise Integration Client for Microsoft Windows 
        -- Delivers packaged software tools for simple and easy 
        integration of Windows NT and OpenVMS.

     *	Systems Management:  OpenVMS Management Tools V2.0 -- 
        Provides data collection tools for performance monitoring of 
        an OpenVMS system from a Windows NT management station, plus 
        the ability to backup or archive data from Windows NT on 
        OpenVMS servers.

     *	Application Development:  Forte WEB Software Development Kit 
        (SDK); CMS Client V1.1; DEC C/C++ V5.5 -- Offers greater 
        integration across development tools for Windows NT and 
        OpenVMS.

     *	Transaction Processing:  Digital Application Generator V3 
        for OpenVMS and Windows NT;  ACMSxp V3.0; RTR V3.0 -- 
        Facilitates the distribution of transactions between OpenVMS 
        and Windows NT, with integrated Internet capabilities.

     *	Mail/Messaging:  MAPI 1 driver for ALL-IN-1 V3.2 --Enables 
        coexistence of ALL-IN-1 and Microsoft Exchange, as well as 
        facilitates migration from ALL-IN-1 to Exchange.
     

     "Windows NT solutions continue to play an increasingly 
important role in enterprise environments, but at the same time, 
there is a growing need for the 24 x 365 availability provided by 
OpenVMS," said Wes Melling, vice president, OpenVMS Systems Group, 
Digital Equipment Corp. "The Affinity for OpenVMS Program enables 
customers to easily address both needs by building on the natural 
affinity between OpenVMS and Windows NT with our growing portfolio 
of solutions for developing, deploying and managing applications 
across both operating systems.  With this third wave of offerings, 
we continue to extend our customers' investments in their OpenVMS 
environments."

Better Support for 24 x 365 Computing with OpenVMS 7.1

     The new release of OpenVMS 7.1 adds greater scalability, 
availability and performance for OpenVMS cluster systems.  With new 
support for Digital's flexible, high-bandwidth, low-latency Memory 
Channel interconnect, OpenVMS cluster systems now offer even greater 
performance and dependability as the enterprise-wide server in a 
three-tier client/server environment.  Also new in OpenVMS 7.1 for 
Alpha and VAX systems are enhancements for connecting OpenVMS 
systems to the Internet, extending VLM64 capabilities, and easier 
systems management of OpenVMS systems.

Expanded Data Warehouse Solutions 

     New capabilities for data warehousing applications, including 
support for VLM64 and VLDB, are now available for OpenVMS.  With 
Data Warehousing on OpenVMS, a relational database serves as the 
data warehouse engine, and an OpenVMS or Windows NT system runs as 
the OLAP (Online Analytical Processing) server accessed by end 
users.  This solution, delivered by Digital with key business 
partners such as Oracle, Sybase, SAS Institute, IBI, Software AG, 
Microsoft and others, provides a scalable, highly available data 
warehouse system, with performance that is up to 250 times faster 
than 32-bit alternatives.

Tighter Enterprise Integration and Management

     The Enterprise Integration Server for OpenVMS and the 
Enterprise Integration Client for Windows NT provide customers with 
the key integration software necessary to connect Windows 
environments to mission-critical OpenVMS applications and data.  
These tools provide out-of-the-box functionality allowing customers 
to instantly begin building an integrated OpenVMS and Windows NT 
environment.

     OpenVMS Management Tools for Windows NT provides a suite of 
tools for managing OpenVMS systems from a Windows NT computer, 
including task-based management of OpenVMS accounts, and printer, 
queue and print job management capabilities.

Integrated Application Development Tools

     New tools let customers more easily develop applications across 
OpenVMS and Windows NT.  Forte WEB SDK for OpenVMS, Windows NT and 
Digital UNIX is an extension to the Forte development environment 
that provides access to enterprise applications from the World Wide 
Web using a standard browser.  Digital's Code Management System 
(CMS) Client for Windows systems allows Windows desktops to access 
CMS libraries and functions that reside on OpenVMS systems.  New 
releases of DEC C and DEC C++ for OpenVMS offer enhanced 
compatibility with Microsoft Visual C++ and provide the flexibility 
to develop applications in a multi-platform environment on OpenVMS, 
Windows NT or Digital UNIX.

Enhanced Transaction Processing

     The Digital Application Generator extends the easy-to-use 
features of Microsoft Visual Basic to allow developers in large 
workgroups and enterprise development environments to design, 
define, prototype, generate and test two-tier and three-tier 
client/server and transaction processing applications cost 
effectively and efficiently.  The new release of ACMSxp provides 
full security and transaction integrity across OpenVMS, Windows NT 
and Digital UNIX.  A new release of Reliable Transaction Router (RTR) 
provides fault-tolerant, transactional messaging middleware for distributed 
client/server applications that require continuous availability, 
transaction integrity and scalable performance.

More Flexible Mail and Messaging

     The new MAPI 1 driver for ALL-IN-1 servers supports the 
coexistence of ALL-IN-1 and Microsoft Exchange. Users of Exchange 
mail clients can process mail and access their document repositories 
on existing ALL-IN-1 servers, further extending the range of mail 
clients supported by ALL-IN-1 and increasing its flexibility and 
usefulness in mixed OpenVMS and Windows NT environments.  Users can 
access both their ALL-IN-1 and Exchange servers, dragging and 
dropping documents from one server to the other, which facilitates 
low-cost, low-risk Exchange deployment.  For customers who have made 
the decision to move to Exchange, the new driver enables the swift 
deployment of Exchange clients, typically the first step in an 
Exchange roll-out.  

     More information is available at http://www.openvms.digital.
com/affinity

     Digital Equipment Corporation is a world leader in open client/
server solutions from personal computing to integrated worldwide 
information systems.  Digital's scalable Alpha and Intel platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace.
