               Digital Expands Its Lead in Delivering
          Total Storage Solutions for Networked Enterprises

MAYNARD, Mass., Nov. 13, 1996 -- Digital Equipment Corporation today 
continued its assault on the market for enterprise storage solutions 
with the announcement of a new high-performance departmental storage 
subsystem -- the StorageWorks RAID Array 450 -- and enhancements to 
its world-class command-and-control software and storage management 
software. The new products augment Digital's comprehensive 
StorageWorks family which includes desktop-to-datacenter storage 
subsystems, disks, optical, tape, adapters, enclosures, and storage 
management software for the most popular multivendor platforms. 

     With a modular architecture that allows customers to use a 
building block approach to storage, command-and-control software 
that lets users manage all of their network storage from a single 
station, and sophisticated storage management software for 
backup/restore, archiving, and Hierarchical Storage Management 
(HSM), Digital is well positioned to address the enterprise storage 
needs of today's open systems market. 

     "With StorageWorks products, Digital offers the most scalable storage 
solutions in the industry," said Dave Coombs, vice president of Digital's 
Worldwide Storage Marketing group. "The products scale from 1 GByte to 
10 TeraBytes, providing a 10,000-fold increase in performance and capacity. 
Enterprise customers can buy only what they need, grow when they want, and 
migrate existing storage to departments or desktops when new technology is 
introduced. No other vendor offers this kind of investment protection.

     "Digital also offers a comprehensive suite of storage 
management software so customers can manage business-critical data 
across multiple platforms. Digital's storage management solutions 
give a company's operations staff the ability to manage data 
anywhere in the world quickly, easily, and cost effectively." 

High-Performance Departmental Storage Subsystem

     The new StorageWorks RAID Array 450 Subsystem brings high 
performance to the departments of corporations, ensuring that 
customers have continuous access to critical data and applications. 
It offers customers a perfect balance between price, high 
availability, and storage expansion, and complements Digital's 
high-performance Enterprise Storage Arrays for large, mission-
critical applications. 

     High-availability features include hot-swappable disks, 
redundant hot-swappable power and cooling, and concurrent support 
for RAID levels 0, 1, 0+1, and Digital's innovative 3/5 
implementation. The StorageWorks RAID Array 450 supports the 
following platforms:  Digital UNIX, Microsoft Windows NT/Alpha, 
Microsoft Windows NT/Intel, Hewlett Packard HP-UX, IBM AIX, Sun 
Solaris, Novell NetWare, and Digital's OpenVMS operating systems. 

     It is available immediately with prices starting at $17,500.

Multi-Platform Command and Control Software

     The StorageWorks Command Console software provides customers 
with an easy-to-use method to configure and monitor StorageWorks 
RAID Array 450 and Enterprise Storage Arrays across the network. It 
is based on an industry-leading graphical user interface, supports 
multiple platforms, and features built-in security and protection. 

     The software enables users to control local and distributed 
storage anywhere on the network from a TCP/IP host system. It allows 
for easy and efficient management of all of a customer's 
StorageWorks resources and is an ideal solution for any company 
looking to minimize costs while improving performance. 

     StorageWorks Command Console software and the license to manage 
a subsystem is included with the StorageWorks RAID Array 450 and 
Enterprise Storage Arrays.  

Sophisticated Storage Management Software

     Today's announcement includes enhancements to a number of 
storage management software products that increase productivity, 
reduce costs, and maintain high data availability.  

     o 	NetWorker Save and Restore V4.2A software provides backup of 
        critical corporate data for Digital UNIX servers, offering 
        customers a 20 percent increase in performance and a 
        reduction in memory and disk space. It features UNIX-to-
     	Windows NT interoperability so customers are free to choose 
        from the broadest range of client platforms in the industry.  
        The software also supports Digital UNIX clusters, Advanced 
        File Systems, Save Set Consolidation, and Oracle databases. 
        NetWorker server software starts at $2,500.

     o 	POLYCENTER Archive/Backup software now provides users with 
        superior archiving and backup in OpenVMS environments. It 
        also supports the backup of UNIX clients, including, HP/UX, 
        Solaris, Sun/OS, AIX, and Digital UNIX, to an OpenVMS 
        server. Prices start at $2,495. 

     o 	POLYCENTER HSM V2.0 separates less frequently used data and 
        stores it near-line, expediting daily backups of heavily 
        used data. It is well suited for mission critical production 
        environments. Prices start at $1,500.

     For more information about Digital's complete line of storage
hardware and software products, call 1-800-STORWORK (1-800-786-7967) 
or visit http://www.storage.digital.com on the World Wide Web. 

