          Digital Equipment Corporation to Resell Worldwide
      PATROL Application Management Products from BMC Software 
 
    
          Expanded Relationship Enables One-Stop Shopping 
     for Application Management Solutions for Digital Customers 


HOUSTON -- Nov. 4, 1996 -- BMC Software, Inc. and Digital Equipment 
Corporation today announced that they have expanded their existing 
relationship with an agreement allowing Digital to resell additional 
BMC Software's PATROL application management products, including all 
PATROL Knowledge Modules (KMs) and the PATROL Consoles. In addition,  
Digital also will offer BMC Software's PATROLVIEW for POLYCENTER and 
PATROLWATCH for Web Browsers products. This announcement enables 
Digital customers to have a complete, tightly integrated solution 
for managing the enterprise, including networks, systems, 
applications and databases.

According to Pauline Nist, Digital vice president of AlphaServer 
Business, "Partnering with BMC and reselling the PATROL products 
enables us to deliver a more complete set of tools to our customers.  
This type of partnership makes sense for both companies by enabling 
each of us to remain focused on our core strengths, while providing 
customers with a complete management solution for mission-critical 
applications and databases running on AlphaServer platforms."

The reseller relationship expands on the agreement signed by Digital 
and BMC Software in January 1996, which initiated the bundling of 
key components of the PATROL product family (the PATROL Agent and 
PATROLWATCH for ServerWORKS) with every AlphaServer system running 
the Windows NT, Digital UNIX and OpenVMS operating systems. The 
relationship now includes the more than 30 PATROL application, 
middleware, application development, database and operating system 
KMs for Digital AlphaServer platforms, as well as additional PATROL 
Consoles. 

"Over the past year, our partnership with Digital has grown and 
expanded, enabling us to offer customers one of the industry's most 
robust and deeply integrated solution sets between an application 
and data management vendor and a hardware platform," said Bob 
Beauchamp, vice president of strategic marketing and corporate 
development for BMC Software.  "This initiative broadens the reach 
of PATROL and helps ensure the health of a customer's business-
critical applications on Digital platforms."

Comprehensive Enterprise Management with PATROL 

PATROL provides comprehensive enterprise-wide management through its 
focus on application and data management solutions. BMC Software's 
PATROL Management Suite optimizes the service provided to users of 
an application by automating and centralizing the control of 
critical elements including data, databases, servers, middleware, 
applications, networks and server hardware.  From a single graphical 
console, the product helps administrators proactively manage all 
systems, ensuring availability and maximum performance 24 hours a 
day. 

PATROL uses server-based Intelligent Autonomous Agents and loadable 
libraries of expertise known as KMs to automatically discover the 
environment; continuously survey the systems; identify and correct 
problems or initiate warnings before they occur; and communicate 
activities as requested from a PATROL Console or a third party 
console via the PATROLVIEW product. 

PATROL supports many leading database platforms, applications and 
middleware, including Oracle, Sybase, Informix, DB2* family, 
Microsoft SQL Server, Oracle Financials, Lotus Notes, the SAP R/3 
System, PeopleSoft Human Resources, TUXEDO, DCE and Transaction 
Server. 

Digital's AlphaServer Leads Industry

Digital's AlphaServer family of systems is the industry's only 
complete line of high-performance 64-bit RISC servers, ranging from 
the AlphaServer 8000 enterprise servers at the high end, to the 
departmental and network AlphaServer 4000 and 2000 class systems, to 
the workgroup and LAN AlphaServer 1000 and 400 platforms. 

Digital offers a balanced choice of processor speed; single-and 
multi-processor symmetric multiprocessing (SMP) configurations; 
64-bit Digital UNIX and OpenVMS operating systems, Windows NT 
operating system; clustering and other high availability features; 
64-bit database support by Informix, Oracle, Software AG, and 
Sybase; and thousands of the most popular applications.

At each price point, AlphaServer systems offer the world's fastest 
microprocessors - up to 437 MHz, huge memory capacity - up to 28GB - 
and storage - up to 3TB, blazingly fast PCI-based I/O, and the 
industry's best hardware warranty.

Availability

The PATROL Management Suite, along with pricing, is available now 
from Digital Equipment Corp. The products will continue to be 
available directly from BMC Software and its agents and distributors 
worldwide. 

About BMC Software

BMC Software, Inc. (Nasdaq:BMCS) is a worldwide developer and vendor 
of more than 100 software solutions for automating application and 
data management across host-based and open systems environments. A 
Forbes 500 company with annual revenues exceeding $425 million in 
fiscal 1996, BMC Software is the world's 11th largest independent 
software vendor and is headquartered in Houston, Texas. For more 
information on BMC Software, access the World Wide Web at 
http://www.bmc.com or call 800.841.2031 or 713.918.8800.

