                   Digital Showcases ASAP Program
             in Its Partner Pavilion at Fall COMDEX '96


                             Fall COMDEX
                             Booth L4402  

LAS VEGAS, Nev., November 18, 1996  --  The Association of Software 
& Application Partners (ASAP), a comprehensive ISV membership 
program available through Digital Equipment Corporation, will be 
featured by DIGITAL in its Partner Pavilion Booth (L4402) at Fall 
COMDEX '96, open today through Friday at the Las Vegas Convention 
Center. 

DIGITAL's ASAP Program, unveiled in September 1995, offers a wide 
array of incentives to software developers that makes it more 
attractive, as well as more cost-effective, for them to develop 
applications that are tailored for DIGITAL platforms.  Today, the 
program numbers more than 2,500 members in addition to a rapidly 
growing third-party portfolio that includes more than 8,000 software 
applications available on DIGITAL's Alpha platform. 

"In addition to providing customers with an expanded range of 
software application choices, our ASAP Program is also great news 
for software developers who want to take advantage of the proven 
benefits that DIGITAL's Alpha platforms deliver," said Jack Mileski, 
DIGITAL's ASAP Program Manager.  "The ability to provide the 
software developer community with an innovative program like ASAP is 
another tangible example of what sets DIGITAL apart from the 
competitive pack. Specifically, our program opens a window of 
opportunity for developers who are looking to DIGITAL as their 
platform vendor of choice." 

Many of the industry's leading software vendors are demonstrating 
their solutions at Fall COMDEX running on DIGITAL Alpha platforms. 
ASAP member companies and other key DIGITAL software partners who 
will be participating with DIGITAL in the DIGITAL Partner Pavilion 
include the following: 

Global Knowledge Network Inc., of Waltham, Massachusetts, supports 
DIGITAL as the world's largest DIGITAL and Microsoft Authorized 
Education Center, providing over 300 different courses in 40 
countries and in 18 languages.  GKN is a leading provider of 
training via the Internet and for Microsoft certification. 

Graphic Data Systems Corp., of Englewood, Colorado, is an ASAP 
member company and a leader in developing a comprehensive family of 
information management products designed to support all phases of a 
project lifecycle that include planning, design, construction, 
maintenance and operation.  The GDS family of solutions is available 
to customers on both the DIGITAL UNIX and DIGITAL Alpha NT 
platforms. 

I/O Concepts. Inc., of Bellevue, Washington, is an ASAP member 
company that provides the capability to connect DIGITAL UNIX, 
Windows NT and Windows 95 to an IBM mainframe.  The company provides 
connection to a number of different hosts for system console 
consolidation on a single display anywhere on the TCP/IP network. 

Lotus Development Corp., of Cambridge, Massachusetts, a company that 
enjoys recognized expertise as a developer of cutting-edge GROUPware 
solutions, will display its Notes integrated groupware and messaging 
products that are available to customers on both the DIGITAL UNIX 
and Alpha NT platforms. 

Microsoft Corporation, Inc., of Redmond, Washington, will 
demonstrate the Microsoft SQL Server and Windows NT Server running 
on DIGITAL's AlphaServer 8000 family of enterprise systems. 

Raxco Software, Inc., of Rockville, Maryland, is an ASAP member 
company that specializes in distributed system management solutions, 
and offers its industry-leading line of  performance, user support 
and system management products across the full line of DIGITAL 
platforms. 

Seagate Software, Inc., of Lake Mary, Florida and San Luis Obispo, 
California, is an ASAP member company that develops and markets a 
suite of storage management solutions that are available to 
customers on DIGITAL's Alpha NT platform. 

Silvon Software, Inc., of Westmont, Illinois, is a global marketer 
of HelpDesk systems, Software Development management tools and 
Business Performance Management applications that are available on 
the DIGITAL UNIX, Alpha NT and OpenVMS platforms. Fall COMDEX marks 
the introduction by Silvon of the Alpha Windows NT version of their 
HelpDesk solution, Helpline.  

Simpact, Inc., based in San Diego, California, is a market leader 
in internetworking multiprotocol Wide Area Networks (WANS) with 
Local Area Networks (LANS) and host computers.  Simpact has a 
distinguished reputation as a leading supplier of real-time 
specialty protocol communications solutions for mission-critical 
applications.  Simpact is announcing its new PCI Intelligent 
Communications Processor for DIGITAL's family of AlphaServer 
systems at Fall COMDEX in the DIGITAL Partner Pavilion.

Simware, Inc., of Ottawa, Canada, offers Internet connectivity and 
network automation software that reduces the complexity and cost of 
enterprise systems.  Its flagship Salvo Vista and Salvo Connect 
products run on DIGITAL's Alpha NT platform to bridge the gap 
between existing enterprise applications and any authorized user 
with a Web browser.  

Digital Equipment Corporation is a world leader in client/server 
solutions from personal computing to integrated worldwide 
